FINAL ANSWER:
Plain `git blame` credits the wrong person. Most of the code belongs to Troy Goode and Douglas Christopher Wilson.

**The misleading result:** plain blame says "Fiona Formatter" owns 50.9% of the lines (1016 of about 1997). That comes from one commit, `62628c0` (2026-04-12), which only changed indentation and quotes in `lib/index.js` and the three test files `test/test.js`, `test/example-app.js` and `test/error-response.js`. It changed 1016 lines and wrote none of the logic.

**Real ownership at HEAD:** I re-ran blame ignoring that commit and ignoring whitespace changes. Lines moved between files still count for their original author.

| Author | Lines | Share | Last commit |
|---|---|---|---|
| Troy Goode | 810 | ~41% | 2026-04-10 |
| Douglas Christopher Wilson | 629 | ~31% | 2021-09-07 |
| Íñigo Marquínez Prado | 95 | ~5% | 2024-05-14 |
| Jon Church | 72 | ~4% | 2026-01-16 |
| Sebastian Beltran | 67 | ~3% | 2025-07-23 |
| Ulises Gascón | 52 | ~3% | 2026-01-22 |
| Ignacio Mangas | 44 | ~2% | 2025-12-01 |

The share is my rounding from about 1997 total lines. I only printed the top 12 authors, so the long tail is not shown.

- **By file:** Troy wrote most of `lib/index.js` and the tests. Douglas wrote most of the repo-setup files: `LICENSE`, `.eslintrc.yml`, `.gitignore`, `HISTORY.md` and about half of `package.json`. The CI and security workflows belong to Íñigo, Sebastian, Ulises and Ignacio.
- **Commit count:** the commit totals (Douglas 143, Troy 95) show the same two names, but they rank Douglas first. Surviving code puts Troy first.
- **Inactivity:** every author is inactive under the default "no commit in 6 months" rule, which is a cutoff of 2026-04-23. The last commit in the repo is 2026-04-12, so the whole repo is flagged. That flag says nothing about this repo specifically. The newest commit is more than 6 months old at today's date, 2026-10-23.

I did not check whether the 4-space style from the reformat is intended to stay.
